<article class="env-definition" id="01WX">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01WX">Definition <span data-tag="01WX">31.15.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $D \subset S$ be an effective Cartier divisor with ideal sheaf $\mathcal{I}_ D$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>invertible sheaf $\mathcal{O}_ S(D)$ associated to $D$</em> is defined by 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{O}_ S(D) = \mathop{\mathcal{H}\! \mathit{om}}\nolimits _{\mathcal{O}_ S}(\mathcal{I}_ D, \mathcal{O}_ S) = \mathcal{I}_ D^{\otimes -1}.  \]
</div>
</li><li><p>
The <em>canonical section</em>, usually denoted $1$ or $1_ D$, is the global section of $\mathcal{O}_ S(D)$ corresponding to the inclusion mapping $\mathcal{I}_ D \to \mathcal{O}_ S$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We write $\mathcal{O}_ S(-D) = \mathcal{O}_ S(D)^{\otimes -1} = \mathcal{I}_ D$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Given a second effective Cartier divisor $D' \subset S$ we define $\mathcal{O}_ S(D - D') = \mathcal{O}_ S(D) \otimes _{\mathcal{O}_ S} \mathcal{O}_ S(-D')$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>